From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:29:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] cheetah: preinstall the KernelSU Next manager

ExpressiveOS ships KernelSU Next in init_boot; the manager is where the user
grants root, installs modules and turns on susfs. It's an unprivileged app
with its upstream signature, which the kernel module checks before trusting
it. ExpressiveOS's expressiveos-cheetah/ksu/fetch-ksu.sh fetches the APK
pinned in ksu.conf and checks its SHA-256 and signer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 device-cheetah.mk |  5 +++++
 ksu/.gitignore    |  1 +
 ksu/Android.bp    | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ksu/.gitignore
 create mode 100644 ksu/Android.bp

diff --git a/device-cheetah.mk b/device-cheetah.mk
index 762825f..36ad4d4 100644
--- a/device-cheetah.mk
+++ b/device-cheetah.mk
@@ -97,3 +97,8 @@ PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     SettingsOverlayStockCheetah \
     SystemUIOverlayStockCheetah \
     WifiOverlayStockCheetah
+
+# KernelSU Next manager (ksu/Android.bp): a normal, unprivileged app. No app
+# gets root until the user grants it here.
+PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
+    KernelSUNext
diff --git a/ksu/.gitignore b/ksu/.gitignore
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..099bedf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ksu/.gitignore
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+KernelSUNext.apk
diff --git a/ksu/Android.bp b/ksu/Android.bp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..40fbd73
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ksu/Android.bp
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+//
+// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Daryl Denson
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+//
+
+// KernelSU Next manager. ExpressiveOS ships a KernelSU Next init_boot (see
+// cheetah/BoardConfig.mk), and the manager is what grants and manages root.
+// The APK isn't in this repo: ExpressiveOS's expressiveos-cheetah/ksu/
+// fetch-ksu.sh downloads the release pinned in ksu.conf and checks its SHA-256
+// and signer, and apply-ksu.sh copies it here. It keeps its upstream
+// signature, which the KernelSU Next kernel module checks before it trusts it.
+android_app_import {
+    name: "KernelSUNext",
+    apk: "KernelSUNext.apk",
+    presigned: true,
+    product_specific: true,
+    dex_preopt: {
+        enabled: false,
+    },
+}
